                                "sense_id": "d7c79c49-17df-3418-b8e2-e4dd95fae18f",
                                "text": "A undescript man hears Brycurs plea, and turns towanrd him:\n\"A magic shop? Oh, yeah, just turn the next 18th corner, go south until you reach a field with pink elephants, chicken with teeth, and flying cows. It's just on the other side of the street...\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f685561-ed33-4cc8-acd7-1da05f6a37af",
                                "sense_id": "d7c79c49-17df-3418-b8e2-e4dd95fae18f",
                                "text": "It could have taken one undescript person with the equivalent of an eraser and the ability to change a map to cause the events to unfurl in Belgrade."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fc0375b0-2774-488b-8434-de73d25dcadb",
                                "sense_id": "d7c79c49-17df-3418-b8e2-e4dd95fae18f",
                                "text": "I'll just leave this vague and undescript because it give it a personal feel, to know that I am talking to each and everyone of you Depeche Mode fans out there!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d643915d-672a-4a59-9c2c-5bd6a753ea7a",
                                "sense_id": "d7c79c49-17df-3418-b8e2-e4dd95fae18f",
                                "text": "So the assertion that man's mythology and the creation (and further modification of) a belief in a deity cannot be refuted as the folly of a species on an undescript planet as illogical? Then refuting any created idea of the recently spawned (claim of) self consciousness by said species on this undescript planet is illogical. Wouldn't you agree?"
